Q-comparison: FLAG — example.py, process_order function, credit limit check
The comparison operator is inverted. At lines:
    remaining_credit = customer.credit_limit - customer.balance
    if discounted_total <= remaining_credit:
        return {"approved": False, ...}

The condition checks if the order total fits within available credit (<=) but then rejects the order. This is backwards. When discounted_total <= remaining_credit, approval should be True. The operator should be > to correctly reject orders exceeding available credit.

